>> title: Miso Salmon Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: salmon, brown rice, miso, japanese, broiler, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: miso salmon bowl, miso glazed salmon, salmon rice bowl, salmon bowl, glazed salmon bowl, rice bowl, grain bowl, protein bowl
>> pairs-with: goma-dare, miso-ginger-dressing
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 20 min
>> slack: unforgiving — a miso glaze under a broiler goes from caramel to charcoal inside a minute, and there is no scraping it back
>> step.1: Salmon is done the moment the flakes part, and it carries on cooking after it leaves the heat. Pull it a minute early.
>> step.2: simmer 40 min, rest 10 min
>> step.3: glaze, then marinate 30 min
>> step.4: broil 7 min, six inches down
>> step.5: macerate 20 min, then drain
>> step.6: build it, salmon in large pieces

Salmon is done the moment the flakes part under a fork, and it carries on cooking after it leaves the heat. Pull it a minute early; you cannot pull it back.

Simmer @brown rice{1 1/2%cups}(280 g; rinsed) in @water{2 1/2%cups}(590 mL) covered ~simmer{40%min}, then ~rest{10%min} off the heat before the lid comes off.

Whisk @white miso{3%Tbs}(50 g), @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @granulated sugar{1%Tbs} and @rice vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL) into a glaze, coat @salmon fillets{4}(6 oz each, skin on) in it and ~marinate{30%min}.

Broil @&(~1)salmon{} skin side down on a #foil-lined sheet pan{} six inches under the element ~broil{7%min}, until the glaze bubbles and catches at the edges and the flakes part at the thick end.

Toss @cucumbers{2}(Persian, sliced thin) with @rice vinegar{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @granulated sugar{1%tsp} and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, then leave them to ~macerate{20%min} and drain.

Spoon @&(~4)brown rice{} into four bowls, lay @&(~2)glazed salmon{} on it in large pieces with @&(~1)cucumbers{} alongside, and finish with @avocado{1}(sliced), @scallions{2}(sliced), @toasted sesame seeds{2%tsp} and @nori{1%sheet}(cut into strips).
